// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_four_bands.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: raster_program's 64-word program buffer (`out.len * 2 <= 128`), which is what
//          caps the number of bands in one program now that parcel P2a has deleted the
//          `restore_n <= 1` count.
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "142 bytes exceeds RASTER_BUF_SIZE"
//
// THIS FILE IS THE SUCCESSOR OF poison_two_restores.emp, renamed rather than deleted, and
// the rename is the honest record of what P2a did. That poison's whole content was TWO
// WELL-FORMED BANDS OVER DISJOINT SPANS whose only defect was the count — and admitting
// exactly that program is what P2a is. A poison cannot survive the deletion of the refusal
// it targets; the only two options were to drop the case (a silent coverage loss at the
// exact spot where a lifted refusal is most likely to stop guarding) or to re-aim it at the
// refusal that INHERITED its job. That refusal is the buffer, and this is that case.
//
// Its old body did not disappear: it is now a POSITIVE fixture in
// engine/effects/raster_dsl.emp (`zz_disjoint`), where it must BUILD through
// raster_program on every build. The two files together are the before and after of one
// deletion — the same program, moved from the expect-fail lane to the must-build lane.
//
// WHY FOUR AND NOT SOME LARGER NUMBER. The cap has to be poisoned at N+1 or it is not
// poisoned at all: a twenty-band fixture would fail for a bound nobody could locate, and
// would keep failing long after the real ceiling had moved. Four is the smallest count the
// buffer refuses, so this case fails if and only if three is the true cap.
//
// THE ARITHMETIC, and it is DERIVED FROM THE SHIPPED op_size rather than from design
// §7.1's table (which is exactly how that table caught the parent spec's stale 14):
// `raster_words` is 7 fixed words — the mask, two priming records, the terminator — plus,
// per fire, 2 + the op_size of its ops. A `band(sh: 0)` over a 1-word `stream_cram` is its
// cheapest possible shape: the ON record is 2 + op_size(Cram, 1 col) = 2 + 6 = 8 and the
// restore record is 2 + op_size(PalRestore) = 2 + 6 = 8, so 16 words per band.
//
//     three bands   7 + 3 x 16 = 55 words = 110 bytes   FITS   (9 words spare)
//     four  bands   7 + 4 x 16 = 71 words = 142 bytes   REFUSED
//
// so the fragment's 142 is this fixture's OWN size and tracks `op_size` in both
// directions, not the 128-byte ceiling. Both halves of that table are pinned as comptime
// facts in engine/effects/raster_dsl.emp's zz_band_ownership_fixtures — including a THREE
// band program that must build through raster_program — so a buffer that GREW would make
// this poison build clean (loud here) and a buffer that SHRANK would break those pins
// (loud there, first). Neither half is sufficient alone: this lane can only prove a
// refusal, and a refusal for a bound that has silently moved reports green.
//
// FOUR TEXTBOOK BANDS. Disjoint one-word CRAM spans at entries 32, 34, 36 and 38, heights
// of 20 lines against a 2-line minimum, eight strictly ascending fire lines 20 apart. The
// ownership walks say NOTHING about this program and that is deliberate: it is the same
// property the file had as poison_two_restores — the only thing wrong with it is the size —
// so a walk that started refusing legal bands would show up as a count of 2 here.
//
// COUNT 1: the buffer ensure alone. Everything else in raster_program passes — the
// intervals are ascending and disjoint, each fire is far under its density gap (20 lines =
// 9760 cycles against ~650 per fire), the frame total is ~5,000 against 84,595, no fire is
// patchable or ships, every restore's fire is single-op, and every band is well formed.
//
// NO IMPORTS, like every ordinary author's module: raster_dsl and engine.vdp are
// COMPTIME_HELPERS members, glob-injected into every module by the real build.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_four_bands

const POISON_FOUR_BANDS = compose([
    band(20,  40,  stream_cram($40, [$0EEE]), 0),
    band(60,  80,  stream_cram($44, [$0AAA]), 0),
    band(100, 120, stream_cram($48, [$0666]), 0),
    band(140, 160, stream_cram($4C, [$0222]), 0),
])

// THE ELABORATION HOOK. A comptime fn is only elaborated when it is CALLED and an
// unreferenced const is inert, so the guard under test runs only because this
// module-level ensure forces raster_program's body. The predicate is deliberately
// trivially-true: the diagnostic under test comes from INSIDE the call, and this
// ensure's own message is what you would see if the poison ever stopped reaching it.
ensure(raster_program(POISON_FOUR_BANDS).len > 0,
       "poison_four_bands: raster_program returned nothing — this poison no longer reaches the guard it targets")
